---
source: crates/trust-cg-test/tests/cli.rs
expression: "help_of(&[\"matrix\"])"
---
Run the workspace unit/integration test matrix (WS1).

Delegates to the maintained full matrix runner in `scripts/run_full_test_matrix.sh`. Writes
`evals/results/tests/<iso-date>.json` with per-crate `{passed, failed, ignored, time_s}`.
Regular-test or rustdoc ignored counts and failed/timeout/incomplete shards make the CLI return exit
1.

# Examples

  trust-cg-test matrix --format human
  trust-cg-test matrix --crate trust-cg-codegen --shard integration-jit-runtime --format json
  trust-cg-test matrix --compare path/to/tests-baseline.json

Usage: trust-cg-test matrix [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --crate <CRATE>
          Only run the named crate (e.g. `trust-cg-codegen`)

  -f, --format <FORMAT>
          Output format (human, json, junit)

          Possible values:
          - human: Pretty table + narrative, targeted at humans
          - json:  Machine-readable JSON
          - junit: JUnit XML for CI consumers

          [default: human]

  -o, --out <PATH>
          Override the command-specific output file or directory.

          See the selected subcommand's help for its output type and default.

      --shard <NAME>
          Shard of a crate to run (e.g. `aarch64`, `macho`). Requires `--crate`

      --since <REF>
          Only run tests changed since the given git ref

      --timeout <SECS>
          Per-unit timeout in seconds. Subcommands may apply per-unit defaults when this is unset

      --compare <PATH>
          Caller-supplied baseline JSON file to diff the run against

      --parallel <N>
          Worker count (honors cargo-serialization lock). Default: auto

  -q, --quiet
          Suppress progress bars; errors still go to stderr

  -v, --verbose...
          Show debug-level events. Repeat for more: -vv, -vvv

      --no-cache
          Ignore proof / corpus caches

      --dry-run
          Print what would run without executing external tools

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
